cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Introduction to Git and GitLab
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Graeme
    family-names: Grimes
    email: Graeme.Grimes@ed.ac.uk
    affiliation: The University of Edinburgh
abstract: >-
  A hands-on introduction to version control with Git and
  GitLab for researchers, analysts and postgraduate students
  who work with data and code but have not used version
  control before. Learners configure Git, record changes
  locally, work with remote repositories on GitLab, use Git
  from RStudio, collaborate in a shared repository, explore
  and restore history, ignore files, and use branches and
  tags. The setup uses University of Edinburgh services, with
  gitlab.com as an alternative.
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ggrimes/gitlab-novice'
url: 'https://ggrimes.github.io/gitlab-novice/'
keywords:
  - git
  - gitlab
  - version control
  - lesson
  - The Carpentries
